    "body": "I have installed `django-filter` to the local environment and made a filter for listings in my project. I gave field names to fields, e.g. `grad` for `city`.\nlistings\\filters.py:\n```Python\nclass ListingFilter(django_filters.FilterSet):\n    city = django_filters.ChoiceFilter(\n        choices=city_list,\n        field_name=\"grad\",\n        lookup_expr=\"icontains\",\n        widget=forms.Select(attrs={\"class\": \"form-select\"})\n    )\n    room_count = django_filters.NumberFilter(\n        field_name=\"broj_soba\",\n        widget=forms.NumberInput(attrs={\"class\": \"form-control\"})\n    )\n    price = django_filters.NumberFilter()\n    price_gt = django_filters.NumberFilter(\n        field_name=\"cena_od\",\n        lookup_expr=\"gt\",\n        widget=forms.NumberInput(attrs={\n            \"class\": \"form-control\",\n            \"placeholder\": \"Od\"\n        })\n    )\n    price_lt = django_filters.NumberFilter(\n        field_name=\"cena_do\",\n        lookup_expr=\"lt\",\n        widget=forms.NumberInput(attrs={\n            \"class\": \"form-control\",\n            \"placeholder\": \"Do\"\n        })\n    )\n    area = django_filters.NumberFilter()\n    area_gt = django_filters.NumberFilter(\n        field_name=\"m2_od\",\n        lookup_expr=\"gt\",\n        widget=forms.NumberInput(attrs={\n            \"class\": \"form-control\",\n            \"placeholder\": \"Od\"\n        })\n    )\n    area_lt = django_filters.NumberFilter(\n        field_name=\"m2_do\",\n        lookup_expr=\"lt\",\n        widget=forms.NumberInput(attrs={\n            \"class\": \"form-control\",\n            \"placeholder\": \"Do\"\n        })\n    )\n\n    class Meta:\n        model = Listing\n        fields = [\"city\", \"room_count\", \"area\", \"price\"]\n```\nFilters used in the form `templates\\partials\\listings\\list\\form.html`:\n```Jinja\n{# Form #}\n<form class=\"border border-secondary-subtle rounded-3 p-3 mb-3\" method=\"get\" novalidate>\n  <div class=\"row mb-3\">\n    <label class=\"col-sm-4 col-form-label\" for=\"city\">Grad</label>\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8\">\n      {{ filter.form.city }}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"row mb-3\">\n    <label class=\"col-sm-4 col-form-label\" for=\"room_count\">Broj soba</label>\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8\">\n      {{ filter.form.room_count }}\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <fieldset class=\"row mb-3\">\n    <legend class=\"col-sm-4 col-form-label\">Cena</legend>\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8\">\n      <div class=\"input-group\">\n        {{ filter.form.price_gt }}\n        {{ filter.form.price_lt }}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <fieldest class=\"row mb-3\">\n    <legend class=\"col-sm-4 col-form-label\">Površina</legend>\n    <div class=\"col-sm-8\">\n      <div class=\"input-group\">\n        <input class=\"form-control\" type=\"number\" name=\"m2_od\" min=\"0\" placeholder=\"Od\">\n        <input class=\"form-control\" type=\"number\" name=\"m2_do\" min=\"0\" placeholder=\"Do\">\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  \n  </fieldest>\n\n  <input class=\"btn btn-primary fw-semibold\" type=\"submit\" value=\"Pretraži\">\n</form>\n```\nWhen I click the submit button of the form, the query parameter have the same names as class properties. `http://localhost:8000/oglasi?city=&room_count=&price_gt=&price_lt=&m2_od=&m2_do=`, but I'd rather have queries be `grad=`, `broj_soba=` and so on. How do I make query parameter names not the same as class property names?",
