    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi, \n\nBack in https://github.com/carltongibson/django-filter/issues/763, there was a brief discussion about whether django-filters could throw a validation error if invalid filters were provided. \n\nFor example, if the FilterSet only allows filtering on the `pizza_name` parameter, and somebody tries filtering on the `foobar` parameter: \n\nmy-api.com/v1/pizzas?foobar=foo\n\nI'd like this to throw a `ValidationError`. Instead it just queries all of the pizzas.\n\nThe response at the time was that it was difficult because:\n\n> [`FilterSets` are] unable to distinguish between undefined filters (description, description__startswith), misspellings (descriptin__cotains), and completely unrelated query parameters (page and page_size for pagination).\n\nI'm curious if this might be worth revisiting. Two reasons:\n\n1. I run the API on CourtListener.com, which is used by hundreds of developers. It's well-documented, but invalid filters are one of the most common problems people have. They set up filters, think they work (no error!), and then seek support when they don't get the results they expect. \n \n    We patiently explain what's going on, and we try documenting our way out of this, but so far only partially succeeded.\n\n2. The second reason is AI vibe coders. In the last few weeks, we've had two AI vibe coders attempt invalid filters on our system. In both cases, serving the requests had a huge impact on our DB as it tried to return all results (millions of items) instead of a filtered set.\n\n    Unfortunately, I don't think we can do much about AI vibe-coders, so we're thinking the best way to fix the issue is to make their bad requests fail.\n\n-----\n\nI'm filing this to see if there's interest in this issue. If so, maybe a mixin or a `StrictFilterSet` object might work to make it a little better. \n\nIt seems like it's be fairly straightforward to create something that could filter out wholly invalid filters, but wouldn't be able to filter out invalid things on the right of the dunder. But even if we can only filter out bad filters minus the dunder, like that would still be a great step in the right direction for us. \n\nI'm curious to hear thoughts. This is something that's irking us more now, thanks to vibe coders, but I know it hasn't been a priority for the package in the past.\n\nThank you for the great package and any thoughts folks have about this.",
